@Access.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5296

# Copie aquí los IDs que devuelven las peticiones para probar las siguientes.
@areaId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@employeeId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Documento OpenAPI con todos los endpoints de la API
GET {{Access.Api_HostAddress}}/openapi/v1.json
Accept: application/json

### Áreas organizacionales
GET {{Access.Api_HostAddress}}/api/areas
Accept: application/json

### RF-01: Registrar empleado
POST {{Access.Api_HostAddress}}/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "documentNumber": "1036123456",
  "firstName": "Ana María",
  "lastName": "Gómez Ruiz",
  "email": "ana.gomez@empresa.com",
  "position": "Auxiliar de bodega",
  "areaId": "{{areaId}}"
}

### RF-01: Registrar empleado con identificación repetida (debe fallar)
POST {{Access.Api_HostAddress}}/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "documentNumber": "1036123456",
  "firstName": "Carlos",
  "lastName": "Pérez",
  "email": "carlos.perez@empresa.com",
  "position": "Vigilante",
  "areaId": "{{areaId}}"
}

### RF-01: Listar empleados (paginado, con filtros opcionales areaId y status)
GET {{Access.Api_HostAddress}}/api/employees?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10
Accept: application/json

### RF-01: Listar solo empleados activos
GET {{Access.Api_HostAddress}}/api/employees?status=Active
Accept: application/json

### RF-01: Paginación inválida (debe fallar)
GET {{Access.Api_HostAddress}}/api/employees?pageSize=-5
Accept: application/json

### RF-01: Consultar empleado por ID
GET {{Access.Api_HostAddress}}/api/employees/{{employeeId}}
Accept: application/json

### RF-01: Actualizar empleado
PUT {{Access.Api_HostAddress}}/api/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "{{employeeId}}",
  "firstName": "Ana María",
  "lastName": "Gómez Ruiz",
  "email": "ana.gomez@empresa.com",
  "position": "Coordinadora de bodega",
  "areaId": "{{areaId}}"
}

### RF-01: Desactivar empleado
PATCH {{Access.Api_HostAddress}}/api/employees/{{employeeId}}/deactivate
Accept: application/json

###
